# Credentials, first and before anything else in this repository exists.
#
# The keytab is the appliance's entire identity: anybody holding it can
# authenticate to the domain as the service account without a password and
# without being prompted. It lives at /etc/cairn-appliance/cairn.keytab on the
# appliance, mode 600, and it must never be anywhere else.
#
# This file was written before the first commit rather than after the first
# mistake. A credential that reaches a repository is not removed by deleting
# it: it is in the history, and the remedy is rotation at the domain rather
# than a commit here.
*.keytab
*.kt
krb5.conf.local
/etc/
secrets/
.env

# What preflight writes when somebody asks it to keep a record. It contains a
# customer's host names and addresses, which is theirs rather than ours.
*.preflight.json
preflight-*.txt

# Go build output.
/preflight/preflight
/preflight/preflight.exe
